'''Kanite''' is a [[Papuan languages|Papuan language]] spoken in [[Eastern Highlands Province]], [[Papua New Guinea]], with a few thousand speakers. One of its dialects is Kagufi.

== Grammatical summary ==
Kanite words are divided into three classes:{{sfnp|Gibson|McCarthy|2002|p=97}}
* Nominal: Words in non-verb phrases with mood suffixes
* Verbal: Words in verb phrases with mood suffixes
* Auxiliary: Words with no mood suffixes

